[{"id":"VRCE-1-33-1","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":33,"verse":1,"english":"And, O Raghava, when Brahmadatta was married, that sonless one, (Kušanābha), with the intention of obtaining male offspring, took in hand a son-conferring sacrifice.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-34-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1033001","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"de9dfa06ec54ade93657012fb9f74dad7054dbb265f2e991dac6281daf4a9a51","compact":"5a15ab5d1c9c78c5843851828897f9cbeb3e75098b9cda47f9d8ac272fb1a31b","nasal":"5a15ab5d1c9c78c5843851828897f9cbeb3e75098b9cda47f9d8ac272fb1a31b"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-33-2","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":33,"verse":2,"english":"And when the sacrifice had commenced, that son of Brahmā, the exceedingly noble Kusa, spoke to king Kusanābha, saying,","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.717,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-34-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1033002","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"573242db02690fbf3feebd294487d67e8f9f25ea86c23ee6edbbd1756d41068d","compact":"e9de228ae00c465e4acff60a3a80fb557315ea8b38cfff62d861efabb0f7d4fd","nasal":"e9de228ae00c465e4acff60a3a80fb557315ea8b38cfff62d861efabb0f7d4fd"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-33-3","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":33,"verse":3,"english":"O son, there will be born to you a virtuous son like to thyself: you will obtain even Gādhi, and through him enduring fame in this world.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.892,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-34-3"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1033003","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"fab30f4ce69a6a66e288c199b739a2afbdcb29fa98af8b98b2d53d42a09f3577","compact":"c8cbe1b0fa6e1c060dbdab1a360f9ee330bb6d1f46efff1e2de39d8f657ad8e0","nasal":"c8cbe1b0fa6e1c060dbdab1a360f9ee330bb6d1f46efff1e2de39d8f657ad8e0"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-33-4","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":33,"verse":4,"english":"Having said this to king Kusanabha, Kusa, O Rāma, entering the welkin, went to the eternal regions of Brahmā.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-34-4"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1033004","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a90124cb4cd696406d6104ec1ae7022e693ecdce0a3abce65c3205a949d9b85f","compact":"4874270be2761266a5dcb49090be39085cd3fcd403e2ec99d411249afd887ade","nasal":"4874270be2761266a5dcb49090be39085cd3fcd403e2ec99d411249afd887ade"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-33-5","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":33,"verse":5,"english":"Then after sometime, an eminently virtuous son, named Gadhi, was born to the intelligent Kusanabha.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-34-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1033005","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"82a0e69cdda38754697251a6c962e813cd26d6360abff41e204de9b4a659599c","compact":"bb78ee4faaaa6234d4fddc58ddfc9bee0030fc0c8d2d7547751d0dd8cfc20017","nasal":"bb78ee4faaaa6234d4fddc58ddfc9bee0030fc0c8d2d7547751d0dd8cfc20017"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-33-6","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":33,"verse":6,"english":"O Kākutstha, even that highly pious Gadhi is my sire. And, O descendant of Raghu, I, called Kausika, am sprung from Kusa's line.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-34-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1033006","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"498fdc28acce2a5a6b5ac515571e4a39c5f7209d83ff9b317d4b0bea75c2c856","compact":"b0360ba4b0bc1b35e86dfdc552b45328515087044139566de154ef787aae571c","nasal":"62f52fe3f0e464ec9b200bd09f76f35bff76811730bb696cb6e20fd877f8fdfb"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-33-7","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":33,"verse":7,"english":"O Rāghava, I had a sister of noble vows born before me. And her name was Satyavatī; and she was bestowed upon Rcīkā.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-34-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1033007","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ff6a825c0aa5c5cb8f31bb17cdf80a755fbfa28334ed99769f46c4966cbc8596","compact":"cb16cc5cda93648fc117059b1dad3b0e81e173480d56b2751064f638b7f1d4e4","nasal":"cb16cc5cda93648fc117059b1dad3b0e81e173480d56b2751064f638b7f1d4e4"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-33-8","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":33,"verse":8,"english":"And following her lord, she ascended heaven in her own proper person. And my highly generous sister, Kausikī, has finally assumed the form of a mighty river.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.464,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-34-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1033008","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"9dd3531b5f0735db3078b7b5e33924164605192a92cafe5713bd2b326f3c0f64","compact":"bf9968076031cece283f96747a8107a5cac6e7d35e15106a2f6221189ff2e362","nasal":"bf9968076031cece283f96747a8107a5cac6e7d35e15106a2f6221189ff2e362"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-33-9","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":33,"verse":9,"english":"And in order to compass the welfare of all creatures, my sister is now a noble and charming river of sacred waters, issuing from the Himavat mountains.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.873,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-34-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1033009","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"fa648bb75fdee8cc579f7513173d0734fec1133b2726cb3ed6b1c6036151ab72","compact":"dffd82b9fef4dca4be6e8e37fc024bae545c82d66d6c43841c9a3332d1a66b29","nasal":"0c84f8880720b3a30f4f0ac955691af858febea4d98da4419b1cb964cba5ad8d"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-33-10","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":33,"verse":10,"english":"And thenceforth, out of affection for my sister, Kausiki, I ever dwell happily in the vicinity of the Himavat, O Raghava.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.641,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-34-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1033010","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"dabc574ea942085829f7eba6114adcc7e8364d7755fa201cdacf019758ce6ad9","compact":"6d10fedfca14d17883cf47445db1b4d7d2cb4e32c31c9167485821bc625b92d5","nasal":"24fb7e85980a2c5e209c91a5fa6ac491db93d8e50e8a3841920574715cd62fb1"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-33-11","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":33,"verse":11,"english":"And that virtuous Kausiki, Satyavati, as well established in religion as truth, and chaste, and eminently pious, is now the foremost of streams.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-34-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1033011","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b48e6167bef9a8e843490a81aeaf99f51fff4632bca1353e0d86370c52229d08","compact":"0b38d7111a47d9fb8ea9adc93131f936408b72856ad183532b82209f1ff941d3","nasal":"0b38d7111a47d9fb8ea9adc93131f936408b72856ad183532b82209f1ff941d3"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-33-12","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":33,"verse":12,"english":"And, O Rama, it is only for the purpose of completing my sacrifice that leaving her behind, I have come to Siddhāśrama. And now by virtue of your energy, have I attained fruition.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.871,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-34-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1033012","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e13b4c2503fc584ae31b76592443a57da550ac81547b028b397570ee67e9ab28","compact":"50715bdddcdf67f0d09f1d9005f17edffe7413308ba65aba3b063ce974aa18d9","nasal":"50715bdddcdf67f0d09f1d9005f17edffe7413308ba65aba3b063ce974aa18d9"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-33-13","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":33,"verse":13,"english":"Now, O Rāma, I have narrated to you the circumstances connected with the history of my line and myself, as also of this place, O mightyarmed one, which you had asked me to relate.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.875,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-34-13"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1033013","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ea7b2412d937cff2e206a50b0b3654164ff55262823ecfab9fbfa4ec21569752","compact":"f83b6841edf1094e312eea67bbb17456b2da1ef3a4c1acaa12bd6da66e259b46","nasal":"f83b6841edf1094e312eea67bbb17456b2da1ef3a4c1acaa12bd6da66e259b46"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-33-14","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":33,"verse":14,"english":"But, O Kākutstha, while I was speaking, half the night has been spent. Do you now sleep, good betide you, so that you may not feel any difficulty while on the journey.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-34-14"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1033014","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"113d175ebc4498b8f8984e69074985ddaea50f71b90d578da429105c485d08a9","compact":"1eef443f1d5c38b33066d51506e44227c8badf31dda7169e1d8c2a4f2148811c","nasal":"1eef443f1d5c38b33066d51506e44227c8badf31dda7169e1d8c2a4f2148811c"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-33-15","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":33,"verse":15,"english":"The trees stand motionless, and the beasts and birds are silent, and, O descendant of Raghu, all sides have become enveloped in nocturnal gloom.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-34-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1033015","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"27f20e9890da311130fba21b1452d8315839a6576f8fe2fe6ad166f7c1c91ccb","compact":"cf9ffc423cd60f904f2dfbba63c48128d8ff12f580263c65fe4067324266b904","nasal":"f706e21eed4ec7b65710355f2c23ad1eb534dbec4c2e04cfe7ec72e71bd65749"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-33-16","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":33,"verse":16,"english":"The noon of night is gradually passing away; and the firmament thick-studded with stars resembling eyes, is illumined up with their light.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.683,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-34-16"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1033016","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c55a4523f19ef8d7f3b61b745d70526ee73a1f00746f0f5e83086ab14f0c7c00","compact":"16946101ba94ae46299b0f5f86f61eb80655e571762486538992079d244432f4","nasal":"16946101ba94ae46299b0f5f86f61eb80655e571762486538992079d244432f4"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-33-17","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":33,"verse":17,"english":"And that dispeller of darkness, the mildbeaming moon is rising, gladdening the hearts of all creatures with his splendour.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.806,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-34-17"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1033017","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c5b98edd8bb82bc4647c6b59935b4a5d4629c155ff63c4ff3173cf6180b0c7b0","compact":"1c8e985b8b6399935cfec2aa74850264be8de986052dddc37aef6e1b90f851c8","nasal":"1c8e985b8b6399935cfec2aa74850264be8de986052dddc37aef6e1b90f851c8"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-33-18","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":33,"verse":18,"english":"And night-ranging being terrible carnivorous Yaksas and Rākşasas—walk here and there,","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.869,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-34-18"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1033018","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"5c4bb866cb0abf52f5468dce4c75258e2e958b570bc4d75ca72436edce426b0d","compact":"54f7850f96da8abaddf46a59f2b1669af49112b140dcb2435638dcb7e8836627","nasal":"c08afcbf5fc01ff52e0e9a969f4a3e7c9c595c1aeb636d9ddfdb88f20a652627"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-33-19","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":33,"verse":19,"english":"Having said this the mighty ascetic of exceeding energy paused. And those ascetics honouring him, said, Excellent! Excellent!","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.667,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-34-19"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1033019","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"84df35ed9bcae0adc1262e9df0f5a8c069d525f1bbdaafb3e831de5265126b67","compact":"68f2d3ced3707280dde1f0dfc896e048c93b838b698914fa322fade4f73d83db","nasal":"68f2d3ced3707280dde1f0dfc896e048c93b838b698914fa322fade4f73d83db"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-33-20","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":33,"verse":20,"english":"Rāma too along with Sumitrā's son having in admiration praised that tiger among ascetics, enjoyed the luxury of slumber.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-34-23"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1033020","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a3202ee9bdfb9213aaf381aaf62524b97455440fbe72a9220048742acfcedbea","compact":"fb7ac1e4dc287ca49b48de47b3e4546cc69ca77e5ef1fb0db6e261d6ae46b84f","nasal":"fb7ac1e4